---
code: records-alien-line
when-fires: a line that is not ours at all appeared in the stream. plan/records.rs admit_records (the strict admission path); the forgiving deframer emits it too. `{count}` is what was seen before the walk stopped.
why: 262 §1 pin-late-and-alien-records: a foreign or stale-attempt writer on the channel; rejected rather than consumed.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork tune --profile web

-- probe-results.txt --
dorc-records/1 nonce=dorc attempt=1 host=localhost book=6b796e0c816aa119a94373a3ab99578a69820f243017ce833973242dd6f9a79e sites=0 @@dorc@@
wombat noise
dorc-records-end/1 nonce=dorc @@dorc@@

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh --results - < probe-results.txt > /dev/null
records: warning[records-alien-line]: sm 1 alien (non-nonce) record line(s)
discarded (counted, never folded)

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: records-alien-line
{{count}} = "1"
